execve - replace a process image and set its environment

SYNOPSIS
    int execve(const char *path, char *const argv[],
               char *const envp[]);

DESCRIPTION
    Both vectors end with a null pointer. argv contains the new program's
    arguments and envp contains name=value strings. A null envp means
    an empty environment. An executable script can specify an absolute
    interpreter after #!, with one optional argument.
    On success the call replaces the caller. On error it returns -1.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), dup2(2), waitpid(2)
